# System Information

## Operating System

The Linux environment used for this laboratory activity is running on a cloud-based Linux playground. It provides a terminal where Linux commands can be executed and tested.

## System Details

The system information was checked using Linux commands. These commands helped identify important details about the operating system, kernel, processor, memory, and storage.

### Commands Used

```bash
uname -a
```

Displays information about the Linux kernel and system architecture.

```bash
cat /etc/os-release
```

Shows the Linux distribution and operating system version.

```bash
lscpu
```

Displays information about the CPU and processor configuration.

```bash
free -h
```

Shows the available and used system memory.

```bash
df -h
```

Displays the available and used disk storage.

## Summary

Using these commands helped me understand how to check and gather system information in a Linux environment. This activity also improved my familiarity with the terminal and basic Linux commands that can be useful when working with cloud computing systems.

